    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $2\\sqrt{3}<3\\sqrt{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt{3}<3\\sqrt{2}$.\n\nExpress the sides as $\\sqrt{12}$ and $\\sqrt{18}$ and compare radicands.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sqrt{3}&=\\sqrt{12}\\\\3\\sqrt{2}&=\\sqrt{18}\\end{align*}$$Since $12<18$, we have $2\\sqrt{3}<3\\sqrt{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Suppose that $n\\geq0$. Prove, more generally, that $n\\sqrt{n+1}\\leq(n+1)\\sqrt{n}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n\\sqrt{n+1}\\leq(n+1)\\sqrt{n}$.\n\nThe radicands differ by $n^2+n\\geq0$; equality holds when $n=0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}n\\sqrt{n+1}&=\\sqrt{n^2(n+1)}\\\\n\\sqrt{n+1}&=\\sqrt{n^3+n^2}\\\\(n+1)\\sqrt{n}&=\\sqrt{(n+1)^2n}\\\\(n+1)\\sqrt{n}&=\\sqrt{n^3+2n^2+n}\\end{align*}$$Since $n\\geq0$, we have $n^2+n\\geq0$, so $n^3+n^2\\leq n^3+2n^2+n$. Taking square roots gives $n\\sqrt{n+1}\\leq(n+1)\\sqrt{n}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
